WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.579
Every Orchard Core site has a home page in its admin.

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:09.796
The Admin Dashboard module replaces it with widgets that you choose and arrange.

00:00:09.796 --> 00:00:15.620
In this video, we enable the dashboard, add and arrange widgets, and decide who sees them.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.621
The dashboard is built from widgets.

00:00:22.621 --> 00:00:26.851
A widget is a content item, so you create, edit, publish, and delete

00:00:26.851 --> 00:00:29.480
it in the same way as any other content.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.992
The dashboard is a grid.

00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:36.161
Each widget has a Position, which sets its order, and a Width and

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:38.393
a Height, counted in grid cells.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:41.270
On a wide screen, the grid has six columns.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.704
The dashboard shows only published widgets.

00:00:44.704 --> 00:00:48.483
A widget that is only a draft, or that you unpublish, stays out

00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:52.700
of the dashboard but remains in the editor, so you can finish it first.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.426
This is the home page of the admin.

00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:04.753
Under Welcome to Orchard Core, cards lead to Create content, Customize theme, Manage

00:01:04.753 --> 00:01:06.410
users, and Learn more.

00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:11.516
To replace it, open Tools, then Features, and search for Admin Dashboard.

00:01:11.516 --> 00:01:14.619
The feature is listed under Content Management.

00:01:16.649 --> 00:01:18.236
Select Enable on its row.

00:01:18.236 --> 00:01:20.949
A message confirms that the feature is enabled.

00:01:21.404 --> 00:01:24.923
Select the site name in the top bar to return to the home page.

00:01:24.923 --> 00:01:28.902
It is titled Dashboard, and a message asks you to click Manage Dashboard

00:01:28.902 --> 00:01:30.024
to add a widget.

00:01:34.254 --> 00:01:36.949
Select Manage Dashboard to open the editor.

00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:41.954
Close Editor leaves it, and Add Widget lists the types of widget that you can create.

00:01:42.405 --> 00:01:48.536
This site has one widget type, Html Dashboard Widget, whose body holds text or HTML.

00:01:48.536 --> 00:01:50.035
Let's choose it.

00:01:50.497 --> 00:01:53.516
Enter a title, and type some text in the body.

00:01:53.516 --> 00:01:56.187
Let's write a short welcome for editors.

00:01:57.744 --> 00:02:02.376
Position, Width, and Height set the place and size of the widget.

00:02:02.376 --> 00:02:06.552
A Position of zero puts it first, a Width of two spans two

00:02:06.552 --> 00:02:09.554
columns, and a Height of one is one row.

00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:14.153
Save Draft keeps the widget out of the dashboard until you publish it.

00:02:14.153 --> 00:02:19.085
Publish adds it to the dashboard and returns to the editor, where the widget appears.

00:02:23.361 --> 00:02:27.783
The editor shows every widget, each with a drag handle beside its title.

00:02:27.783 --> 00:02:31.014
Let's drag Office hours by its handle to the front.

00:02:31.014 --> 00:02:32.941
The other widgets make room.

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:36.318
The order is saved as soon as you drop the widget.

00:02:36.318 --> 00:02:41.980
A message says that the dashboard was successfully updated, and Undo restores the previous arrangement.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:47.716
To resize a widget, drag its right edge, its bottom edge, or its bottom right corner.

00:02:47.716 --> 00:02:50.441
Let's drag the corner of Style reminders.

00:02:50.441 --> 00:02:52.470
It snaps to whole grid cells.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.858
The size is saved the same way.

00:02:54.858 --> 00:02:58.731
You can also type the values in the Position, Width, and Height fields

00:02:58.731 --> 00:03:00.362
of the widget's edit form.

00:03:00.835 --> 00:03:03.330
Each widget has an Actions menu.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.795
For a published widget, it offers Edit, Delete, and Unpublish.

00:03:08.275 --> 00:03:15.115
A draft, such as Holiday schedule, offers Publish Draft and Discard Draft instead of Unpublish.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.084
Select Close Editor.

00:03:17.084 --> 00:03:21.912
The dashboard shows the published widgets in the order and sizes that you set.

00:03:21.912 --> 00:03:26.050
Holiday schedule is a draft, so it stays out until you publish it.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.744
Two permissions control the dashboard.

00:03:32.744 --> 00:03:36.316
Access the Admin Dashboard lets a user see the dashboard.

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:42.270
Manage the Admin Dashboard adds the Manage Dashboard button, and it includes the access permission.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:46.724
By default, the Administrator role has both permissions.

00:03:46.724 --> 00:03:51.743
The Editor, Moderator, Author, and Contributor roles can access the dashboard.

00:03:51.743 --> 00:03:57.300
You change the permissions of these four roles on the Roles page, under Access Control.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:01.558
Access to the dashboard is not enough to see a widget.

00:04:01.558 --> 00:04:07.172
A user who cannot manage the dashboard also needs permission to view the widget's content.

00:04:07.172 --> 00:04:11.850
If no widget is left to see, that user gets the welcome home page instead.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.315
Widgets come from content types.

00:04:18.315 --> 00:04:23.501
To make your own, create a content type under Design, Content Definition, Content

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:26.900
Types, and enter DashboardWidget as its Stereotype.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.913
Add parts such as a title and a body.

00:04:29.913 --> 00:04:33.702
The type then appears under Add Widget, and a part that stores the

00:04:33.702 --> 00:04:35.860
position and size is added for you.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.855
That's the Admin Dashboard module:

00:04:39.855 --> 00:04:43.896
a start page of widgets that you arrange for your editors, with permissions

00:04:43.896 --> 00:04:45.492
that decide who sees what.

00:04:45.492 --> 00:04:46.790
Thanks for watching.

